{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ולא אמרו שלום לו", :translit "v'lo am'ru shalom lo", :gloss "and they did not say shalom to him"} {:he "כי אין שלום אמר אלוה לרשעים", :translit "ki ein shalom amar elohah lar'sha'im", :gloss "for there is no shalom, said Elohim, to the wicked"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Textual contrast: the verse says 'they said shalom' without the phrase 'to him,' implying they withheld shalom from the wicked Laban."}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'there is no shalom, said Elohim, to the wicked' is drawn from Isaiah 48:22 and Isaiah 57:21, both of which state 'ein shalom, amar Elohim, larsha'im.' The midrashic tradition applies this declaration to Laban: Bereishit Rabbah 70:3 records that since Laban was wicked, the shepherds of Haran did not pronounce shalom upon him, explaining why the verse states only 'and they said shalom' without the words 'to him.'", :sources ["Isaiah 48:22" "Isaiah 57:21" "Bereishit Rabbah 70:3"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Textual contrast: the verse says 'they said shalom' without the phrase 'to him,' implying they withheld shalom from the wicked Laban.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:08:57.444024752Z", :model "glm-5.2"}